.TH zeshij 1  "zeshij 0.1.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
zeshij \- Smart session manager for Zellij
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBzeshij\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Smart session manager for Zellij, a port of sesh. Every command goes to the zeshij plugin: inside Zellij through `zellij pipe`, outside through a short\-lived bridge session; there the terminal shows Zellij only for the picker and for the session it connects to. Without a command, zeshij opens the picker.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBzeshij connect [OPTIONS] <TARGET>...\fR
.RS 4
Connect to the given session (aliases: cn)
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-switch\fR
Switch the session (rather than attach); zeshij always moves the client, as sesh does from inside tmux
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-command <CMD>\fR
Execute a command when connecting to a new session. Will be ignored if the session exists
.TP
\fB\-r, \-\-root\fR
Connect to the git root of the target
.TP
\fB<TARGET>\fR
Alias, session name, layout, config entry, path or zoxide query
.RE
.TP
\fBzeshij last\fR
.RS 4
Connect to the last session (aliases: L)
.RE
.TP
\fBzeshij list [OPTIONS]\fR
.RS 4
List sessions (aliases: l)
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-config\fR
Show configured sessions
.TP
\fB\-t, \-\-tmux, \-\-zellij\fR
Show Zellij sessions, live and exited
.TP
\fB\-z, \-\-zoxide\fR
Show zoxide results
.TP
\fB\-T, \-\-tmuxinator, \-\-layout\fR
Show Zellij layouts
.TP
\fB\-H, \-\-hide\-attached\fR
Don\*(Aqt show the current session
.TP
\fB\-d, \-\-hide\-duplicates\fR
Hide duplicate entries
.TP
\fB\-b, \-\-blacklisted\fR
Show blacklisted sessions
.TP
\fB\-i, \-\-icons\fR
Show icons
.TP
\fB\-j, \-\-json\fR
Output as json
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-no\-color\fR
Show icons without color (requires \-\-icons); also drops the colors of \-\-format
.TP
\fB\-\-icons\-exclude <SOURCES>\fR
Don\*(Aqt show source icons for these session sources (for example: zellij,zoxide)
.TP
\fB\-\-format <FORMAT>\fR
Format each session row ({name}, {session}, {source}, {path}, {active_window_name}, {active_window_name_prefix}; colors: {fg:yellow}...{/fg})
.RE
.TP
\fBzeshij mkdir [OPTIONS] <PATH>\fR
.RS 4
Create a directory and connect to it as a session (aliases: md)
.TP
\fB\-s, \-\-switch\fR
Switch the session (rather than attach); zeshij always moves the client
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-command <CMD>\fR
Execute a command when connecting to the new session
.TP
\fB<PATH>\fR
The directory to create (`mkdir \-p`); a relative path starts from the current directory
.RE
.TP
\fBzeshij preview [OPTIONS] <NAME>\fR
.RS 4
Preview a session or directory (aliases: p)
.TP
\fB\-w, \-\-watch\fR
Continuously refresh the preview; zeshij prints one frame (use `watch \-c`)
.TP
\fB\-\-interval <DURATION>\fR
Refresh interval when watching [default: 500ms]
.TP
\fB<NAME>\fR
A name printed by `zeshij list` (also with the glyph of `\-i`) or a directory
.RE
.TP
\fBzeshij root [PATH]\fR
.RS 4
Show the root name of the current session, or of PATH (aliases: r)
.TP
\fB<PATH>\fR
A directory; required outside Zellij
.RE
.TP
\fBzeshij picker\fR
.RS 4
Interactive session picker (the default command) (aliases: pick, pk)
.RE
.TP
\fBzeshij completion <SHELL>\fR
.RS 4
Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
.TP
\fB<SHELL>\fR
The shell to complete [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
